     sections=[["Two economies, one marketing problem", "<p>Nashville runs on two economies at once. The visitor economy fills Broadway, the honky-tonks, the convention calendar and a bachelorette schedule that seems to run twelve months a year. The resident economy is the one exploding underneath it: one of the largest healthcare hubs in the country, a country music industry that employs far beyond the stage, and neighborhoods like East Nashville and The Nations filling with new residents and new businesses every quarter. Most Nashville companies sell to both, and marketing built for only one side leaves money on the other.</p>"], ["The full mix, one team", "<p>The usual failure here is not effort, it is hand-offs. A media buyer chasing the tourist dollar, a web firm that has never thought about the local customer, a social freelancer posting into the void, and the strategy living in nobody&rsquo;s head. Extra Medium runs the whole system under one roof: strategy first, then digital, SEO, paid media, social, creators, content, creative and web, measured against revenue. When the gap is the leadership seat itself, a <a href=\"/fractional-cmo-nashville/\">fractional CMO in Nashville</a> sits inside your company and owns the plan week to week.</p>"], ["Senior people, price in writing", "<p>Extra Medium is founder-led and senior-only, built on two decades in local media and startups and influencer marketing run at scale for large brands. The person in the first meeting is the person doing the work; there is no account layer learning on your budget. Every engagement starts the same way: the shape and the price in writing before work begins, so you can judge the commitment before you make it. Our <a href=\"/how-much-does-a-marketing-agency-cost/\">marketing agency cost</a> page shows how that pricing usually breaks down.</p>"]],
